  "body": "Small findings of the post audit against the LinuxCNC manuals (#4130). None changes what the machine runs.\n\n1. The measure check writes `M2` with no `#<_task>` guard (`assets/posts/linuxcnc.cps:1065-1069`, `:1088`). In the preview the probe value is not real, so a large deviation can end the backplot early. Guard the check with `#<_task> EQ 1`.\n2. The comment guard (`linuxcnc.cps:359-360`) does not catch keywords with spaces (`M S G`) or `PYRELOAD`, so such a name can show as an operator message. Ignore whitespace in the test and add `PYRELOAD`.\n\nEvidence: upstream/main `f0bdc5109`.\n\nDone means: each item is fixed with a test, or closed with a reason in a comment.\n",
